          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्वीकारणे — svīkārṇe — \"to accept\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "त्याने नवीन नोकरी आनंदाने स्वीकारली. tyāne navīn nokrī ānandāne svīkārlī. He gladly accepted the new job."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with -ने (he …): त्याने स्वीकारलं, tyāne svīkārlaṁ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Transitive: the past agrees with what is accepted, नोकरी स्वीकारली."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्वीकारणे (svīkārṇe) is built on the tatsama स्वीकार, Sanskrit svīkāra, \"making one's own, accepting\" (Monier-Williams), with the verb ending -णे."
            }
          ]
        },
